@meta
id: 25-06
title: Drill — delete the line that says it
chapter: 25
type: drill
skills: range-pattern
par: 18
minutes: 4
reps: 8
vscode: Ctrl-F, Escape, Home, shift-Down, Delete
open: errors.json

@brief
Eight times: the `PAYMENT_LEGACY_DECLINED` code was retired with the old
gateway. Delete its line from the cursor on line 1, without moving.

Name the line by its pattern, not by its number.

@keys
| `:/LEGACY/d` | delete the next line matching `LEGACY` |

@hints
One address, one command. The address is the search.
--
`:/LEGACY/d` Enter, `:wq`.

@solution
    :/LEGACY/d<Enter>  :wq<Enter>

Fifteen keystrokes. Speed is not the point of this drill; not looking at
the gutter is. When you can delete a line you can see without working out
which number it is, you have stopped navigating and started describing,
and every later command in this chapter takes the same description.

Pick a fragment that is unique and short. `LEGACY` is six characters and
matches one line; `PAYMENT` matches four.

@start errors.json
{
  "ORDER_NOT_FOUND": { "statusCode": 404, "sentry": false },
  "ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED": { "statusCode": 409, "sentry": false },
  "BATCH_PAYLOAD_INVALID": { "statusCode": 422, "sentry": false },
  "PAYMENT_LEGACY_DECLINED": { "statusCode": 402, "sentry": false },
  "PAYMENT_REFUND_FAILED": { "statusCode": 502, "sentry": true },
  "PAYMENT_GATEWAY_TIMEOUT": { "statusCode": 504, "sentry": true },
  "CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND": { "statusCode": 404, "sentry": false }
}

@expected errors.json
{
  "ORDER_NOT_FOUND": { "statusCode": 404, "sentry": false },
  "ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED": { "statusCode": 409, "sentry": false },
  "BATCH_PAYLOAD_INVALID": { "statusCode": 422, "sentry": false },
  "PAYMENT_REFUND_FAILED": { "statusCode": 502, "sentry": true },
  "PAYMENT_GATEWAY_TIMEOUT": { "statusCode": 504, "sentry": true },
  "CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND": { "statusCode": 404, "sentry": false }
}
